      ":question/id": "3a558acd-0b05-5aa8-b518-45323798923a",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-125086",
      ":question/problem": "Find $a+3b$ if $a=8i-5j$ and $b=-3i+2j.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To compute $a+3b,$ we just need to compute all of the $i$'s and $j$'s, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+3b & =(8i-5j)+3(-3i+2j) \\\\  & =8i-5j-9i+6j \\\\  & =(8i-9i)+(-5j+6j) \\\\  & =-i+j\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
