      ":question/id": "d15383e5-4c36-54f6-9a69-8b61467023e3",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-125088",
      ":question/problem": "Find $3a-2b$ if $a=-2i-2j$ and $b=4i-3j.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To compute $3a-2b,$ we just need to compute all of the $i$'s and $j$'s, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a-2b & =3(-2i-2j)-2(4i-3j) \\\\  & =-6i-6j-8i+6j \\\\  & =(-6i-8i)+(-6j+6j) \\\\  & =-14i+0j \\\\  & =-14i\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    }
